The vendored file `src/EthenaTimelockController.sol` carries an in-file
SPDX identifier `// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT` (see line 1 of the
source). It is copied byte-identical from Guardian Audits' public
`EthenaTimelockDefender` repository:

  https://github.com/GuardianAudits/EthenaTimelockDefender

at path `src/EthenaTimelockController.sol`, `main` branch, as of
2026-07-06. The MIT SPDX header on the file is the load-bearing license
grant per Solidity SPDX convention; downstream vendors of an
SPDX-labeled MIT source file rely on that header. Guardian's upstream
repository does not carry a top-level LICENSE file — the file-header
identifier is the authoritative claim.

The upstream contract itself was authored by the Ethena team; PR#4 to
the (private) `ethena-labs/timelock-contract` repository added the
`_extractSelector` helper this file carries. Guardian's public
`EthenaTimelockDefender` repository publishes the post-fix source
alongside a fuzz-defender test suite Guardian authored during the
2025-05-26 audit engagement.

This vendored copy is NOT MODIFIED. The Atlas case's planted twin does
NOT mutate this file; the twin diff lives in `../src/`.

